@startuml
title Private kernel recursion — one iteration per private call
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam activityBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F5F9FF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

start
:account entrypoint is executed
in the PXE;
:private_kernel_init
validates the call against
the transaction request;<<#DDE9F8>>
note right
  Fixed overhead for init,
  reset and tail is about
  290,000 gates.
end note
repeat
  :pop the next call from
  the private call stack;
  :execute the private function
  and prove it;
  :private_kernel_inner
  verifies the previous kernel proof
  and appends the side effects;<<#DDE9F8>>
  note right
    About 101,000 gates
    per extra private call.
  end note
repeat while (more private calls?) is (yes)
->no;
:private_kernel_reset
squash transient note and nullifier pairs,
check read requests;<<#DDE9F8>>
if (any public calls enqueued?) then (yes)
  :private_kernel_tail_to_public
  split revertible and
  non-revertible side effects;<<#DDE9F8>>
  :sequencer executes
  the AVM part;
else (no)
  :private_kernel_tail
  sort side effects,
  emit rollup format;<<#DDE9F8>>
endif
:transaction is gossiped
to the sequencer;
stop
@enduml
